1	//! EAGLE-3 speculative-decoding gate (greedy, one request per draft round).
2	//!
3	//! Greedy speculation must be lossless: every committed token is the target's
4	//! own pick, so the output matches plain greedy decode up to the benign
5	//! prefill-vs-decode tie flips that `common::lossless` tolerates. The tests
6	//! also read the engine's speculative counters, so a run that should draft
7	//! fails when it silently decodes plainly. Losslessness does not check the
8	//! draft forward itself: the verifier rejects a wrong draft, which only lowers
9	//! acceptance.
10	//!
11	//! Requires a CUDA GPU, Qwen3-4B weights and an EAGLE-3 drafter for it (e.g.
12	//! `AngelSlim/Qwen3-4B_eagle3`). Set `PEGAINFER_TEST_MODEL_PATH` (target) and
13	//! `PEGAINFER_EAGLE3_TEST_MODEL_PATH` (drafter); the tests skip when either is
14	//! absent. The two engines run one after the other so only one target is
15	//! resident at a time.
16	
